    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW25gNRrBAMuP7KHa4qEqWBeG)_\n\n**Before:** `sp-clean-whitespace` (the command asked about as `sp-remove-whitespace`) ran from the global `before-save-hook`. `sp-backups` saves modified buffers after 5 s idle (`lem-full-auto-save`, plus `auto-save-visited-mode`), and those saves run the same hook. In the middle of writing, the cleanup stripped the space just typed at the end of a line and collapsed blank lines around point, which in Org moved text and broke words.\n\n**After:** the hook calls `sp-clean-whitespace-before-save`, which skips the cleanup in the modes of the new option `sp-clean-whitespace-autosave-skip-modes` (default `(org-mode)`, derived modes included) unless the save was explicit (`this-command` is `save-buffer`, `save-some-buffers` or `write-file`). Set it to `nil` to restore the old behaviour. `M-x sp-clean-whitespace` is unchanged. Module doc and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n**Not tested:** nothing was run (no Emacs in the container). Saves from other commands (e.g. Magit's save prompt) count as non-explicit in Org buffers.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01B9aoaHQtTqhFb4gp4BAvQM)_",
